            "invisible": false,
            "solution": ""
          },
          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Marie Curie's Early Life</strong><br>\nMaria Sklodowska, known as Marie Curie, was born on November 7, 1867, in Warsaw, Poland. She was the youngest of five children in a well-educated but financially struggling family. Despite the challenges, including the loss of her mother and sister at a young age, Marie was a top student in her secondary school. Unfortunately, her gender barred her from attending the University of Warsaw, which was male-only at the time.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Education and Early Scientific Work</strong><br>\nMarie Curie moved to Paris to pursue her education at the Sorbonne, where she earned degrees in physics and mathematics. She met Pierre Curie, a professor of physics, at the School of Physics and they married in 1895. Together, they began conducting research on radioactive substances. Their partnership was both romantic and scientific, with each contributing to groundbreaking work in radioactivity.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Discovery of Radioactivity</strong><br>\nCurie's pioneering research led to the discovery of radioactivity, a term she coined to describe the spontaneous emission of radiation by an atom. She observed that certain substances, like uranium, emitted rays that were able to penetrate solid materials. This finding was crucial for the development of atomic physics and changed the way scientists understood the structure of the atom.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
